# Changelog

## 0.4.0 — 2026-10-12

- Read-only workout schemas and validated strength-step builder with explicit units.
- Paginated exercise search with exact matches and explicit variant selection;
  catalog omissions never trigger substitution.
- Strength workflow skill. 198 tests passed; a synthetic strength template was
  saved, verified and deleted.

## 0.3.1 — 2026-10-12

- Terminal OAuth approval displays actual scopes and explicitly distinguishes
  read access from permission to modify the account. Reject requests changed
  while the owner reviews consent.

## 0.3.0 — 2026-10-12

- Queryable write schemas and durable status, fresh calendar/device/type/health
  verification reads, complete activity edit templates and exercise catalog search.
- All-operation schema/type validation; unit/date/DST/FIT-range checks, upload
  integrity and decoded activity-file checks with the official Garmin FIT SDK.
- Target/device/catalog preflights, duplicate scheduling and foreign-set guards;
  terminal rejected outcomes explicitly distinguish no mutation from unknown.
- Block SDK account-mutation replay after HTTP 401. Partial import failures remain
  unknown with preserved successful identifiers and no automatic retry.
- Account-management skill and updated workout skill/documentation. Live audit
  tested all 16 exposed operations, all three upload formats, and cleanup.
  Delayed imports, one failed manual variant and physical-device limitations documented.

## 0.2.0 — 2026-10-11

- Scheduling preparation now returns specific local-validation errors for names,
  ID types and date formats, distinct from upstream write failures. Added exact
  SDK scheduling arguments to MCP tool guidance.
- Added a discoverable workout creation/scheduling skill to Garmin Connect,
  with SDK schema guidance, a validated example, and safe verification workflow.
- Reject malformed workout enums and duration/distance fields, including nested
  repeat steps, before preparing standalone or calendar writes. Unknown write
  results now include a safe error category without upstream messages or secrets.
- Consent pages provide a fully quoted command using the running installation's
  absolute Python path, with no environment activation or directory change.
- Registrations that omit scope now support requesting read and write. Tokens
  still carry only locally approved authorization scopes; existing clients and
  explicitly read-only registrations remain unchanged.
- Corrected protected-resource discovery to advertise optional write scope while
  retaining read-only minimum authentication and existing read grants.

- Opt-in preview/commit tools with 16 fixed write operations: workouts,
  scheduling/removal, device push, manual activities, bounded FIT/TCX/GPX uploads,
  activity edits, strength sets and health measurements.
- Dated workout batches for calendars (not native Garmin Coach plans).
- Encrypted intent journals, expiry, duplicate protection and partial progress;
  no application-level mutation retries or read-cache reuse.
- Separate garmin:write grants; existing grants remain read-only.
- Workout template reads, validation tests and branch/PR/merge contribution flow.

## 0.1.0 — 2026-10-11

Initial public release:
- Seven bounded, read-only Garmin activity and training tools over MCP stdio.
- Interactive login and MFA; Windows DPAPI session encryption.
- Local Codex plugin and interpreter-aware Windows installer.
- Optional ngrok HTTPS access with OAuth, PKCE, local consent, refresh rotation
  and revocation. Owner verified access in ChatGPT on a phone.
- Offline tests and Windows/Linux CI; current ChatGPT callback-ID support.

Limits: unofficial Garmin API; personal single-owner remote service; PC must
stay online. Remote setup is tested on Windows. ChatGPT mobile availability
depends on the account and workspace.
